  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "In the sky of Iron Eagle blessed land, twelve eagle nests of peculiar shape hold precious rank eight immortal materials. After those twelve nests are all lost, ripples appear in the air and a thirteenth eagle nest appears, drawing every immortal’s attention.",
      "chapters": [
        1109
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_iron_eagle_blessed_land"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Chu Du appears, blocks the immortals, and deters them in order to obtain this nest. He one-shots Green City Rampage’s giant form, slaps Modest Thatched Hut aside, and places the thirteenth eagle nest into his own immortal aperture.",
      "chapters": [
        1109
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "chu-du-seizes-the-nest",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_chu_du",
        "move_green_city_rampage",
        "house_modest_thatched_hut"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Hei tribe’s first supreme elder later shouts that Chu Du has taken the thirteenth eagle nest and that Hei Fan true inheritance is inside it.",
      "chapters": [
        1110
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "chu-du-seizes-the-nest",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_hei_tribe",
        "inh_hei_fan_true_inheritance"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The nest is usually concealed and only appears when Iron Eagle blessed land is near the point of breaking apart. Inside are clues to Hei Fan’s true inheritance. After the battle of Hei tribe, Chu Du snatches it under Fang Yuan’s guidance, then meets Fang Yuan secretly. Fang Yuan obtains flying sword Immortal Gu and the eagle nest while lending out calamity beckoning Immortal Gu.",
      "chapters": [
        1114
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "transfer-to-fang-yuan",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "sys_immortal_gu",
        "gu_calamity_beckoning_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "In Mini Purple Heaven the nest floats as a crystal structure like a three-storey building with no doors or windows. Its outer nest alone contains five hundred kilograms of rank eight heavenly crystals, and its value surpasses the sum of all the other eagle nests. Narration identifies it as the thirteenth eagle nest from Iron Eagle blessed land, the nest Chu Du took at the final moment of Hei tribe’s battle after collaborating with Fang Yuan.",
      "chapters": [
        1115
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "heavenly-crystal-form",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_mini_purple_heaven"
      ]
    }
  ],
